You should independently review important code, infrastructure changes, security configurations, financial information, legal information, production deployments, and other high-impact outputs before relying on them.

## 5. Agentic and Autonomous Actions

ORVYN may include autonomous or semi-autonomous agents capable of performing actions on your behalf, including:

- reading and modifying project files;
- executing terminal or shell commands;
- running tests and builds;
- accessing development environments;
- interacting with websites or browsers;
- connecting to servers;
- using SSH or remote execution;
- deploying applications;
- interacting with APIs and connected services;
- installing or invoking tools, skills, plugins, or MCP servers; and
- operating cloud or sandbox environments.

Certain actions may require your approval depending on your selected access mode, permissions, organizational policies, or the assessed risk of the action.

You remain responsible for the environments, credentials, servers, repositories, accounts, and resources that you authorize ORVYN to access.

Kernel AI Labs may restrict, require confirmation for, or refuse actions that present elevated security, safety, infrastructure, compliance, or operational risk.

## 6. Access Modes and Permissions

ORVYN may provide configurable access levels such as read-only, approval-required, balanced, autonomous, or full-access modes.

Your selected access mode determines the level of authority ORVYN may exercise within supported environments.

Certain high-risk or destructive actions may require explicit approval regardless of the selected access mode.

You are responsible for selecting appropriate access levels for your projects, servers, organizations, and users.

